WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:02.519
The whole flow at a glance

2
00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:06.693
Type Create experiment in the palette (Ctrl+P)

3
00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:11.628
A title creates the experiment folder and README

4
00:00:11.628 --> 00:00:16.606
The workflow view lists the new experiment as planned

5
00:00:16.606 --> 00:00:21.176
Find it in the palette by its English name

6
00:00:21.176 --> 00:00:24.626
Pick a workflow from the catalog

7
00:00:24.626 --> 00:00:28.703
Give it an alias to create the workflow note

8
00:00:28.703 --> 00:00:32.108
The experiment row now shows workflow progress

9
00:00:32.108 --> 00:00:45.471
Insert a unit operation into the workflow

10
00:00:45.471 --> 00:00:50.516
Open the Samples view: no DNA samples yet

11
00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:59.144
Type @DNA; under Input to reference a sample

12
00:00:59.144 --> 00:01:13.345
Alias, description and location give it a new ID

13
00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:20.614
The new DNA sample is in the Samples view

14
00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:25.328
In the workflow view it is still planned

15
00:01:25.328 --> 00:01:35.046
Change the experiment status to in-progress

16
00:01:35.046 --> 00:01:38.261
The experiment moved to the in-progress group

17
00:01:38.261 --> 00:01:48.584
Stuck? Open user guide opens QUICKSTART
